                    {
                        "form_id": "8c2b9d99-f99b-4346-bd6e-310e23f48e61",
                        "entry_id": "7badff5d-cc62-3aca-9dfe-eb7c56190390",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "и́зморосях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e3689777-bb41-3437-ac45-a4915e7a0b98",
                        "entry_id": "7badff5d-cc62-3aca-9dfe-eb7c56190390",
                        "glosses": [
                            "очень мелкий, моросящий дождь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b3eaa45-5f25-436f-a743-efccf91a736e",
                                "sense_id": "e3689777-bb41-3437-ac45-a4915e7a0b98",
                                "text": "День был пасмурный, начиналась изморось…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01e1ec25-5d30-405e-9897-45a46f7711ea",
                                "sense_id": "e3689777-bb41-3437-ac45-a4915e7a0b98",
                                "text": "Конечно, наши сентябрьские вечера, особливо под конец месяца, не то чтоб пленяли особенною приятностью; конечно, и изморось грустная, мелкая и холодная дребезжит в окно; конечно, и город представляет неприятный вид с поднятыми шинелями пешеходов, с их зонтиками, калошами и прочим дрязгом…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14633018-03d3-41c3-93e3-3d47f14c6d10",
                                "sense_id": "e3689777-bb41-3437-ac45-a4915e7a0b98",
                                "text": "Конденсация пара была так велика, что влага непосредственно из воздуха оседала на землю мелкой изморосью."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "625c05a5-3bb7-46e5-85a9-9e0977e33715",
                        "source_entry_id": "7badff5d-cc62-3aca-9dfe-eb7c56190390",
                        "source_sense_id": "e3689777-bb41-3437-ac45-a4915e7a0b98",
                        "target_lang_word": "drizzle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "drizzle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31a062ff-e88c-3803-bb0c-7bd0dcc61b79",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rain lightly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "impersonal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "650a3c6e-e759-4905-9a91-9d7eb1217a21",
                                                "sense_id": "31a062ff-e88c-3803-bb0c-7bd0dcc61b79",
                                                "text": "We had planned a picnic for Joe's birthday, but it ended up drizzling all day."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b705362f-9172-3e91-bf5e-bb1e61aa005b",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shed slowly in minute drops or particles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be64af0f-bcd8-41db-a27f-4c2a493b5ca4",
                                                "sense_id": "b705362f-9172-3e91-bf5e-bb1e61aa005b",
                                                "text": "And from mine eyes the drizling teares descend,\nAs on your boughes the ysicles depend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc061c63-f8ce-44bf-a1c1-9df33bad8260",
                                                "sense_id": "b705362f-9172-3e91-bf5e-bb1e61aa005b",
                                                "text": "When the sun sets, the air doth drizzle dew;\nBut for the sunset of my brother’s son\nIt rains downright."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fddc1e0-e59e-363a-8fbf-3641122aacda",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pour slowly and evenly, especially oil or honey in cooking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3b2cda-b81d-465b-afff-7c9f42786929",
                                                "sense_id": "4fddc1e0-e59e-363a-8fbf-3641122aacda",
                                                "text": "The recipe says to toss the salad and then drizzle olive oil on it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "787350dd-bcc2-3b52-9871-cf739660d22a",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover by pouring in this manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c03990b-e099-4518-b353-22992c275731",
                                                "sense_id": "787350dd-bcc2-3b52-9871-cf739660d22a",
                                                "text": "The recipe says to toss the salad and then drizzle it in olive oil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04760fad-4e2c-3a3a-9ee0-a5e23349a87c",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To urinate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a57d303-7f63-47f5-ac51-20153f01f91a",
                                                "sense_id": "04760fad-4e2c-3a3a-9ee0-a5e23349a87c",
                                                "text": "She'll be right back, had to drizzle before we leave."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c8d51fa-1c64-3844-aee5-985195dbf035",
                                        "entry_id": "c833c2f0-2e1c-3117-bf6c-e0d5a2f9c126",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To carry out parfilage, the process of unravelling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32e0c6f6-fc52-43e2-a918-5a51d1369a40",
                                                "sense_id": "6c8d51fa-1c64-3844-aee5-985195dbf035",
                                                "text": "She found that all those ladies who did not play at cards occupied their fingers with parfilage.[...] Here, the work was called drizzling. Ladies begged their friends to give them pieces of the gold lace used on uniforms and the gold tassels of sword-belts, they picked out the metal threads, and by selling these they realised considerable sums. Prince Leopold himself drizzled continually[...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "drizzle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94f4dc66-f573-320d-ad7d-5f13642e39b0",
                                        "entry_id": "a793945a-c72d-3d73-bfbc-dcd88f0656d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Light rain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26d365f7-9b7f-4722-a4ac-79a392479b24",
                                                "sense_id": "94f4dc66-f573-320d-ad7d-5f13642e39b0",
                                                "text": "Up here, it's a 'dreich' day with steady drizzle. Deep drainage channels either side of the track are already more like streams: Rannoch Moor is a wet place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd02c57b-84b1-36fa-b0aa-c84e3cd0adba",
                                        "entry_id": "a793945a-c72d-3d73-bfbc-dcd88f0656d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very small, numerous, and uniformly dispersed water drops, mist, or sprinkle. Unlike fog droplets, drizzle falls to the ground."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08088136-cf6d-4b20-86af-62b24ff13dff",
                                                "sense_id": "dd02c57b-84b1-36fa-b0aa-c84e3cd0adba",
                                                "text": "No longer pouring, the rain outside slowed down to a faint drizzle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2bcbcc3-803d-3cb6-91be-1f035200aaf3",
                                        "entry_id": "a793945a-c72d-3d73-bfbc-dcd88f0656d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "349233d2-60e8-463c-9e29-79277a13bcbf",
                                                "sense_id": "f2bcbcc3-803d-3cb6-91be-1f035200aaf3",
                                                "text": "Stop drinking all of my drizzle!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb2bf7d7-9af3-3567-80a0-c083eee2b593",
                                        "entry_id": "a793945a-c72d-3d73-bfbc-dcd88f0656d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cake onto which icing, honey or syrup has been drizzled in an artistic manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbbcf1e8-7c8c-41f2-ba87-4a9847a6134a",
                                                "sense_id": "fb2bf7d7-9af3-3567-80a0-c083eee2b593",
                                                "text": "April 19, 2013,Felicity Cloake, \"How to Cook the Perfect Lemon Drizzle Cake\" in The Guardian\nDrizzle is not normally good news. Not when it's falling from the sky, not when it's replacing a decent helping of sauce, and especially not when it's found on a menu in close proximity to the words \"balsamic vinegar\". Deliciously sticky, sweet and sour lemon drizzle cake is the one, and very honourable, exception."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f48ea154-f39d-4fb1-87db-bace7ffb5be7",
                                                "sense_id": "fb2bf7d7-9af3-3567-80a0-c083eee2b593",
                                                "text": "The rest of the day is spent trying to concentrate on ingredient labels, ordering supplies, baking some fairy cakes for a hen party and two lemon drizzles, one for a new baby and one for an old dear's birthday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
